  "summary": "Build implemented all three phases of the ordinary-text autocomplete plan in the working tree, with named obligations still open. BaseComboboxPlugin, triggerCombobox and the four input schemas are deleted; mention, slash, emoji and footnote queries stay ordinary editor text. Matching policy is each feature plugin's ComboboxState in initialState, which cut the planned combobox() contribution. One private owner per mounted Editable opens an occurrence only on a locally typed trigger, picks the latest trigger across mounted popups, bounds the query with range anchors, takes Enter, Tab, arrows and Escape before the shortcut table while its popup shows, ends on another editor's focus, and writes the Editable's combobox ARIA. useCombobox({ plugin, editableRef, open, onKeyDown, activeOptionId }) returns the match and complete(match, callback), which settles native input, rechecks the offered query and replaces trigger and query in one refusable new-batch update. Plite gained a public ReactApi.settleInput(); the v54 converter migrates stored inputs to literal trigger and query text; the copied popups, docs, doctrine v255, changesets and generated registry output follow. Copilot keeps its auto-trigger beside an open popup. Open: native-owner review of settleInput and content-root key arbitration, emulated and physical IME proof, several browser cases and the typing benchmark, each tracked in the autocomplete decision page. This outcome supersedes 2026-10-01-autocomplete-ordinary-text-adoption-execution after the plan moved its last self-tracked gates to the decision page and the spec gained a remote-edit mapping case.",
  "proof": {
    "state": "partial",
    "evidence": [
      {
        "path": "packages/platejs/src/react/features/combobox/useCombobox.spec.tsx",
        "sha256": "43c49b0d02e3384c3cf2e5a822a6708633f512b6fb3a27b3c68e69bc005b9856",
        "claim": "useCombobox spec, 16 of 16 on these bytes: activation on a typed trigger, inside one longer insertion and across formatted leaves, with the latest trigger winning when one insertion holds two; no popup for a caret placed after a trigger or a trigger followed by whitespace; the occurrence ends past the typed text, on dismissal, on same-change trigger replacement and when another editor takes focus, survives and maps through a remote edit before the trigger, and stays closed after Escape through a remote edit and a caret return; keys stay with the editor while hidden, reach the open popup before the shortcut table, and Shift chords stay with the editor; refusal, a stale match, a thrown callback and a returned promise leave no edit; completion is one undo step, undo restores the literal query and caret without reopening, and redo restores the completion."
      },
